  "transcript": "Sometimes it's less work to just do the task. I can use AI to build something that does it for me, but if it breaks or the way I wanna do the job changes, I am still the one who's gotta go back and fix it. Say I automate how I organize files for a project. If I'm still moving folders around and changing what goes where, I've now gotta update the automation as well. For something I do all the time, that might be worth it. But if it's an occasional job and I'm still figuring out how I want it done, I might be better off leaving it manual for now. You guys tell me, what's something you've deliberately kept doing yourself because the automation wasn't worth looking after?",
